# Written into every graphify-al search_dir as `.graphifyignore` before a
# graph build (see incremental.py::_ensure_graphify_ignore).
#
# graphify-al is a general-purpose, multi-modal knowledge-graph tool, not
# AL-specific -- by default it extracts "document" nodes from .md/.txt/etc.
# files right alongside real AL code nodes. Found live (2026-07-03): a real
# tester's query seeded on a bogus node literally labeled 'Codeunit "SFTP
# Client"', sourced from a README.md heading, not the real SFTP Client
# codeunit's actual AL declaration -- the graph had 431 such doc-sourced
# nodes total. This project's graph is meant to be the exact structural AL
# code relationship graph (constitution: calls/subscribes/extends); docs
# are already served separately via the search corpus (chunker/), so
# mixing document-prose nodes into the same graph only pollutes seed
# selection with non-code matches. Exclude everything graphify recognizes
# as non-code (its own DOC_EXTENSIONS/PAPER_EXTENSIONS/IMAGE_EXTENSIONS/
# OFFICE_EXTENSIONS/VIDEO_EXTENSIONS, graphify/detect.py) so only real
# AL/code files (graphify's own CODE_EXTENSIONS, which includes .al)
# become graph nodes.
*.md
*.mdx
*.qmd
*.txt
*.rst
*.html
*.yaml
*.yml
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.svg
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mkv
*.avi
*.m4v
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.ogg
